 "text": "Hey, nice to hear from you. How are you? Not at all. Many people start then and find it doable. A few hours a week go a long way. That's half the fun. Which language are you looking at, and why? Portuguese would give you real-life language use, Greek is beautiful. Which ever you go with, start with the basics every language uses, like saying hello and saying goodbye. There are lots of approaches. Apps like Duolingo are nice for getting used to the interface. Books like The 7 Languages of Love are great for seeing grammar around sentences. For now, start with one approach and switch if you find one isn't working.",
